# CH16 — The Engine That Waited. Cinderwake's assembly yard: channels, space, the Iron Tortoise, the manual, the launch.

@scene CH16_YARD once
say narr | The old assembly yard. On the slipway lies a hull - broad, ugly, bolted rather than grown. The Golem is under it with a lamp.
say ivo | Morwen. Elowen. Raven. Aurex. ...You're here. You're here and I'm leaking oil everywhere.
say tessa | You found a ship.
say ivo | I found a ship nobody finished. Rescue vessel, drafted before heartglass made everything 'efficient'. Steam and gears. Heavy. Slow.
say ivo | Her name's Lanternwake. The engine works. I've tested every part twice. It just needs the cooling channels powered and room to fit the stabilisers.
say oriel | And?
say ivo | And the hull twists on the slipway. Nothing I've got is heavy enough to hold her straight while we bolt the keel.
objective ivo | Power the three cooling channels (valves on the north wall), then help the crews clear the assembly space.
@end

@scene CH16_IVO
if flag:t03y_ch1,flag:t03y_ch2,flag:t03y_ch3 powered
say ivo | Three valves on the north wall. The channels have to run cold before the engine can breathe.
end
label powered
if flag:t03y_clear cleared
say ivo | Channels are cold! Now the crews can shift the scrap - talk to the crew chief.
end
label cleared
say ivo | Space is clear. Now all we need is something that can hold a ship straight. Something very heavy and very patient.
@end

@scene CH16_CHANNEL1
if flag:t03y_ch1 done
sfx FX010
set t03y_ch1
say narr | The west valve opens. Water hisses into the channel; the pipe frosts white.
call CH16_CHANNELS
end
label done
say narr | The west channel runs cold.
@end

@scene CH16_CHANNEL2
if flag:t03y_ch2 done
sfx FX010
set t03y_ch2
say narr | The middle valve opens with a shudder. The channel under the slipway starts to sing.
call CH16_CHANNELS
end
label done
say narr | The middle channel runs cold.
@end

@scene CH16_CHANNEL3
if flag:t03y_ch3 done
sfx FX010
set t03y_ch3
say narr | The east valve opens. Steam coils out of the vents and thins to nothing.
call CH16_CHANNELS
end
label done
say narr | The east channel runs cold.
@end

@scene CH16_CHANNELS
if flag:t03y_ch1,flag:t03y_ch2,flag:t03y_ch3 all
end
label all
objective ivo | The channels are cold. Talk to the crew chief about clearing the assembly space.
@end

@scene CH16_CREW
say worker | Channels are running cold - we can work the yard now. Scrap on both sides, and a few rust-crawlers nesting in it.
say worker | You handle the crawlers, we handle the scrap. Deal?
battle D04P_1
fade out 0.4
say narr | The crews haul, stack and sort for an hour. The assembly space opens up around the hull.
set t03y_clear
fade in 0.4
say worker | Space is clear. Now - what's that at the east end? It wasn't there this morning.
objective ivo | Something very large is waiting at the east end of the slipway.
@end

@scene CH16_TORTOISE
say narr | A tortoise the size of a cottage, its shell plated like a boiler. It has been watching the hull for some time.
say tortoise | I held up this yard's roof in the old days. Under orders. They called me a foundation.
say tortoise | Nobody has ordered me since the bell. So I came to see whether anyone would ask.
say ivo | ...Would you hold the hull straight while we bolt the keel? You can stop whenever you like. We'll brace it with jacks as we go, so it doesn't depend on you.
say tortoise | You asked. And you built it so it does not need me.
say tortoise | Then I will help. And afterward I will go where I like - which is, I think, with you.
fade out 0.6
say narr | The Iron Tortoise leans its shell against the hull. The crews bolt the keel in one long afternoon, jacks going in behind every bolt.
fade in 0.6
set v06_given
vestige V06
say ivo | ...Now the manual. Pell's going to ask.
@end

@scene CH16_PELL
say pell | Golem. Before you take her anywhere. The manual.
say ivo | It's in my head.
say pell | That's the problem. Write it down. All of it. Every valve, every spare, every noise she makes when she's sick.
say ivo | That's weeks of work -
say pell | Then we'll wait weeks. I'm not watching another machine that only works when one engineer stands beside it.
wait 0.4
say ivo | ...You're right. You were right about the wheel, too.
fade out 0.6
say narr | The Golem writes for three days. Morwen checks every page. The crews read it aloud and argue with it, and the Golem changes it where they're right.
fade in 0.6
key K_MANUAL
say narr | The manual lies on the workshop bench, heavy and dog-eared. Anyone can pick it up.
call CH16_LAUNCH
@end

@scene CH16_BENCH
if flag:v06_given bench
say narr | A workbench covered in the Golem's calculations. Very little of it is legible to anyone but the Golem.
end
label bench
if ch:CH16 manual
say narr | The workbench, waiting for a manual.
end
label manual
say narr | The Lanternwake manual, dog-eared, with a pencil tied to it on a string. The newest note, in a crew hand: 'Page 12 is wrong. Fixed.'
@end

@scene CH16_LAUNCH once
music silence
say narr | Launch morning. The crews take their places - not the Golem. The Golem stands at the back, plated hands folded, runes dimmed.
still ST11_launch
say worker | Page one. Cooling channels open.
say worker | Open.
say worker | Page two. Boiler to working pressure. Slow.
say worker | Slow. Holding.
say worker | Page three. Release the slipway brakes.
sfx FX031
shake 0.5
music M019
say narr | Lanternwake slides down the slipway and lifts, heavy and steady, into the smoky sky over Cinderwake.
say ivo | ...I didn't touch anything.
say tessa | You wrote it down. That's touching everything.
join C04
chapter CH16
vehicle ship true
airship home
objective dain | Lanternwake waits at Hearthward's berth. Find Vespera (High Aerie), Sak (Veyr) and Oni (Whitebone) - in any order.
rumor | High Aerie's broken chain now links two new islands. A cliff settlement there is evacuating.
rumor | Veyr's throne square is a distribution point. Someone is guarding the lower registry from Voss's remnants.
rumor | Whitebone's old cells are a sanctuary now. People with bindings nobody can safely remove shelter there.
level_floor 28
@end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Cinderwake (post)
@scene T03P_PELL
if ch:CH16 after
say pell | Power fails in patches now. We rotate heat workshop by workshop. The clinic never goes cold - that's the one rule.
say pell | The Golem's in the old assembly yard east of here. He says he found a ship. He also says he's fine. He's lying about one of those.
end
label after
if ch:CH20 q04
say pell | The manual's on every bench in town now. People argue with it in the margins. That's how you know it's alive.
end
label q04
call Q04_HOOK
@end

@scene T03P_ROTA
say worker | Heat rota: canteen at dawn, clinic always, workshops by turn. We post it on the wall under the injury tally.
@end

@scene T03P_CLINIC
say monk | The clinic's warm. That was the question you all asked, back when. Here's the answer: we share.
@end

@scene T03P_TALLY
say worker | The tally wall. We kept counting after the bell. Fewer marks since the regulators went dark. Make of that what you like.
@end

@scene T03P_CHILD
say child | The pipes don't sing anymore. The waterwheels squeak instead. I like the squeak better.
@end

@scene T03P_WHEEL
say worker | Waterwheels at every terrace. Slower than the regulators. Nobody's inside them.
@end

@scene T03P_CANTEEN
say baker | Shift stew. Same as ever. Except now there's a waterwheel keeping it warm instead of a - well. You know.
shop SHOP_T03
@end

@scene T03P_INN
say keeper | Cots by the canteen stove. Take a shift on the wheels if you want. Or don't. Rest.
inn 0
@end
